=== VERDICT ===
  fault class : bad_deploy
  fix class   : rollback
  confidence  : medium
  evidence    : tr_451a0f2a493a, tr_ee1f8a8e0866, tr_a84d740b0da4, tr_d029746e7b7d
  root cause  : At 20:52:55 platform-automation pushed an image-reference update on the ad service to an ad-hotfix tag [tr_451a0f2a493a], and one second earlier the running ad JVM logged a complete, orderly gRPC shutdown and then went permanently silent — no startup, bind or listen lines ever follow through window close [tr_ee1f8a8e0866]. The replacement artifact never came up. Frontend traces show the consequence: the lone error chain terminates at frontend's outbound gRPC call to ad GetAds, a childless leaf failing in ~1ms, i.e. a connection-level refusal rather than ad-side logic or a timeout [tr_a84d740b0da4]. Frontend has no change of its own to blame [tr_d029746e7b7d]. The artifact running on ad is not one that serves traffic.
  OPEN        : No pod or container-state evidence was gathered: ImagePullBackOff, CrashLoopBackOff, or never-scheduled all produce this symptom and were not distinguished.
  OPEN        : The ad metrics query covered a window ending ~18 hours before onset [tr_a851199a2db8], so its 'ad is not the origin' conclusion is not actually measured against the incident.
  OPEN        : The ~5 minute gap between ad's shutdown at 20:52:54 and the 20:58:01 onset is unexplained, and the breadth of the 8-service blast radius is unaccounted for by the single error path found.

